WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.520
Welcome to Grade 7 English, Unit
1: Family, Identity, and History.

2
00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:08.580
This is Unit 1: Family, Identity, and History.

3
00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:16.300
In this unit, you will explore some of the most important
questions a person can ask: Where do I come from?

4
00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:18.560
Who are the people in my family?

5
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.320
What stories have been passed down through the generations?

6
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:27.500
You will read about families, learn
how to describe your own background,

7
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:33.900
and discover how people across East Africa
and the wider world have moved, settled,

8
00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:36.460
and built new lives over the centuries.

9
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:43.260
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

10
00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:50.700
By the end of this unit, you will be able to read and
understand a passage about family history and migration,

11
00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:53.320
and discuss its ideas in English.

12
00:00:54.220 --> 00:01:00.100
You will also use the past simple tense correctly
to describe completed actions and events.

13
00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:06.280
You will also distinguish between the
past simple and the present perfect tense.

14
00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:09.260
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

15
00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:18.040
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: accumulation,
accuracy, administration, advancement, ballad, fable.

16
00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:24.160
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

17
00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:27.760
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

18
00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:37.180
The reading sequence includes Keeping the Story Alive:
Oral History and Heritage and The Journey of Alina's Family.

19
00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:38.960
Read actively.

20
00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:44.840
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

21
00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:49.280
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

22
00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:53.500
The first language focus is The Past Simple Tense.

23
00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:59.620
The past simple tense describes actions and
events that started and finished in the past,

24
00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:01.980
which makes it the storyteller's tense.

25
00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:07.660
Almost every sentence in a biography, a
family history or a chronicle depends on it,

26
00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:11.180
so this unit treats it as your most important tool.

27
00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:18.260
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

28
00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:24.200
In speaking, you will complete Speaking
1: Present Your Family Biography.

29
00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:29.660
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

30
00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:33.960
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

31
00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:37.580
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

32
00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:39.000
You are ready to begin.

33
00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:45.520
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

34
00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:48.220
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

35
00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:55.280
Use the AI tutor for hints and feedback any time, and
bring your questions to a live session too if you join one.
